      "current_title": "Ask HN: Is web programming a series of hacks on hacks?",
      "excerpt": "Been doing application development, primarily backend development, for a number of years. I've always found it quite easy to move up and down the stack and work anywhere from UI down to the bare metal in a number of environments and languages, and always the 'fast learner' who quickly knows the system inside-out, even when thrown into some area that I've never seen. Lately I've been doing some web development on a fairly long-lived and large code-base, but I'm finding it MUCH",
